---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="FileLocker Privacy Policy | Local File Processing" 
  description="Read the FileLocker Privacy Policy to learn how your data and files are handled when using our browser tools for password protection and encryption online."
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <div class="guide-hero">
    <div class="hero-shape hero-shape-1"></div>
    <div class="hero-shape hero-shape-2"></div>
    <div class="hero-inner" style="text-align:center; max-width:40rem;">
      <h1>FileLocker Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle" style="margin:0 auto;">
        FileLocker is designed to process selected files locally in your browser rather than uploading them to a FileLocker server.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- MAIN CONTENT -->
  <div class="w-full bg-[#f8fafc] py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">

      <div class="content-card animate-fade-in-up flex flex-col gap-8 divide-y divide-gray-100">
        
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 sm:gap-6 pt-2">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-14 h-14 bg-green-50 rounded-[1rem] flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="w-7 h-7 text-green-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" /></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2 mt-1">Local File Processing Without Uploads</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
              FileLocker is designed as a <strong>client-side application</strong>. This means that all of the complex password-protection math happens directly inside the memory of your web browser. 
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-xl mt-3">
              FileLocker does not use a server to receive selected files for processing. If the page and required resources are already loaded, processing can continue without an active internet connection.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 sm:gap-6 pt-8">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-14 h-14 bg-blue-50 rounded-[1rem] flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="w-7 h-7 text-blue-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z" /><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M2.458 12C3.732 7.943 7.523 5 12 5c4.478 0 8.268 2.943 9.542 7-1.274 4.057-5.064 7-9.542 7-4.477 0-8.268-2.943-9.542-7z" /></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2 mt-1">Your FileLocker Password Stays in Your Browser</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
              Because password processing happens locally in your browser, your FileLocker password is not sent to a FileLocker server during file protection. FileLocker does not store or recover your password if you lose it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 sm:gap-6 pt-8 pb-2">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-14 h-14 bg-purple-50 rounded-[1rem] flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="w-7 h-7 text-purple-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0zM12 14a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z" /></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2 mt-1">No Account Required for File Protection</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
              You don't need to sign up or create an account to use FileLocker. The browser-based file protection tool is designed to let you password protect files and folders without requiring an account or storing a password for you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
